{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.sameColumn_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.sameColumn_count","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L153-L184","doc":"**The same-column count is the row index.** For the column-superstandard tableau,\n`#{j < s : (j s) ∈ colStab}` equals the row of `s`'s cell.\n\nThe bijection sends `j` to its row. It lands in `range (row s)` by\n`sameColumn_filter_eq`; it is injective because a label is determined by its cell and\nthe column is pinned; and it is surjective because a Young diagram is down-closed in\ncolumns (`YoungDiagram.up_left_mem`), so every row below `s`'s in the same column is\noccupied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.sameColumn_filter_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.sameColumn_filter_eq","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L137-L151","doc":"The `colStab` filter is exactly a (same column, smaller row) condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.colPattern_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.colPattern_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L123-L125","doc":"`colPattern` of the column-superstandard tableau is the cell's column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.swap_mem_colStab_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.swap_mem_colStab_iff","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L112-L121","doc":"**Same column ↔ the transposition stabilises the column pattern.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lt_iff_row_of_sameCol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lt_iff_row_of_sameCol","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L94-L104","doc":"Within a fixed column, label order is row order. The specialisation of\n`lt_iff_colRow` that the same-column count consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lt_iff_colRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lt_iff_colRow","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**The defining property — column-major.** Label `l` precedes `m` iff `l`'s cell is in an\nearlier column, or the same column and an earlier row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lt_iff_key","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lt_iff_key","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L79-L83","doc":"Label order is exactly lex-key order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.key_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.key_apply","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L74-L77","doc":"The lex key of label `l`'s cell is exactly `lexIso`'s value at `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.colSuperstandard","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L69-L72","doc":"**The column-superstandard tableau**: label `l` sits at the `l`-th cell in\ncolumn-then-row order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexIso","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The order isomorphism `Fin (nOf μ) ≃o lexCells μ` — labels in increasing key order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexCellsEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexCellsEquiv","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L61-L63","doc":"Transport back: a lex key in `lexCells μ` is a cell of `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexCells_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexCells_card","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.lexCells","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The cells of `μ`, carried into the lex synonym where the order lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.swapLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.swapLex","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardTableau.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Cell `(row, col)` ↦ lex key `(col, row)`. Composing `prodComm` with `toLex` puts the\ncolumn first, so the lex order on keys is exactly \"column-major, then row\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}